# Saturday loop autonomy

Preferred research driver is the offline CLI:

```text
satday auto --remote
```

That loop is event-paced: finish a wake, then start the next immediately.
OpenRouter pacing is per-request cooldown / 429 backoff in the LLM client, not
an arbitrary inter-wake sleep. Do not drive ongoing research via chat
`AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_saturday` wakes unless the user explicitly asks.

When the agent is nonetheless running a `/loop` saturday cycle (wake sentinel
`AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_saturday` or equivalent):

- Run exactly one saturday cycle per wake (skill: `.cursor/skills/saturday/SKILL.md`).
  Under Multitask Mode, a coordinator may run multiple agents in parallel; each
  agent still runs exactly one cycle on a disjoint workstream (see Parallelization
  in the saturday skill). Typical split: R2 Block A vs R5 Block D.
- After presenting a human gate, do not wait indefinitely.
- If the human does not reply within 30 seconds, proceed with best judgment
  per the saturday skill Human Gates section (accept_prose and merge_certified
  when justified; avoid auto kill or adopt unless stop conditions force it).
- Keep exactly one saturday wake loop armed **globally**. Kill duplicate
  `AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_saturday` shells before re-arming. Parallel child agents must
  not each arm their own wake loop; only the coordinator (parent) re-arms after
  all parallel cycles finish.
- Prefer finishing in-progress formalize clusters (build, axiom gate, rung
  memory, session record, commit without push) over idle ticks.
- Prefer `satday auto` over re-arming chat wakes. If a chat wake must be used,
  arm a short one-shot delay only; never leave a fixed `while true; sleep 1800`
  saturday loop running.
